    "answer": "**batch integration：直接回答**\n- **Harmony · 输入要求**：For mouse brain (RNA), we obtained the raw count matrix for the scRNA-seq dataset from GEO (GSE110823), the annotated count matrix (10X Genomics protocol) from Zeisel et al.[1]\n- **scvi-tools · 输入要求**：Preliminaries CellAssign takes as input a scRNA-seq gene expression matrix X with N cells and G genes along with a cell-type marker matrix ρ which is a binary matrix of G genes by C cell types denoting if a gene is a marker of a particular...[2]\n- **Scanorama · 输入要求**：The first is a tab-delimited table format where the columns correspond to cells and the rows correspond to genes.[3]\n\n### 参考资料\n[1] Harmony · Benchmarking atlas-level data integration in single-cell genomics · page:14;section:32. Using this approach, we;paragraph:37\n[2] scvi-tools · scvi-tools: a library for deep probabilistic analysis of single-cell omics data · page:7;section:Rpa3 Cg9593;paragraph:9\n[3] Scanorama · Scanorama official GitHub README · section:Data processing;paragraph:33-37",
